/* This driver's only hard requirement on the network buffer pool.
 *
 * The RX descriptor's buffer is the netpkt's own data area -- there is no
 * bounce buffer and nothing is copied -- so the buffer size the DMA is
 * programmed with is CONFIG_IOB_BUFSIZE itself.  It has to hold a maximum
 * Ethernet frame (1518 bytes including the VLAN header the MAC may pass) and
 * it has to be a whole number of DMA beats.  The ethernet configuration uses
